<title>INDIA: India approves TMT flowers project.</title>
<headline>India approves TMT flowers project.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian Industry Ministry said on Friday that it approved a plan by TMT India Ltd to set up a wholly-owned, export-oriented unit to cut flowers in the southern state of Karnataka.</p>
<p>It said the plan involved the issue of 1.6 bln rupees' worth of preference shares.  </p>
<p>It said in a statement that the plant, in the state capital Bangalore, would have an annual capacity of 108 million flowers.</p>
<p>It said the plant expected to export 5.28 billion rupees' worth of flowers. It did not disclose the time period for the projected exports.</p>
<p>- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
